# Pocket Hydra: Multi-Tool + BLE Hardware Wiring Guide

This document outlines the pinout and wiring schematics required to integrate the multi-tool module with an ESP8266 (NodeMCU) running the Pocket Hydra firmware extension.

---

## 1. OLED Display (SSD1306 - I2C)
| Display Pin | ESP8266 GPIO / Pin | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **GND** | GND | Ground |
| **VCC** | 3V3 | Power (3.3V) |
| **SCL** | D1 (GPIO 5) | I2C Clock |
| **SDA** | D2 (GPIO 4) | I2C Data |

---

## 2. HM-10 Bluetooth BLE Module
| HM-10 Pin | ESP8266 GPIO / Pin | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **VCC** | 3V3 / 5V | Power (dependent on module regulator) |
| **GND** | GND | Ground |
| **TX** | D5 (GPIO 14) | SoftwareSerial RX |
| **RX** | D6 (GPIO 12) | SoftwareSerial TX |

---

## 3. CC1101 Wireless Modules (SPI)
Both CC1101 modules utilize the shared hardware SPI bus, separated by individual Chip Select (CSN) pins.

| SPI Signal | ESP8266 GPIO / Pin | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **GND** | GND | Ground |
| **VCC** | 3V3 | Power (Must be strictly 3.3V) |
| **MOSI** | D7 (GPIO 13) | Shared SPI MOSI |
| **MISO** | D6 (GPIO 12) | Shared SPI MISO |
| **SCLK** | D5 (GPIO 14) | Shared SPI Clock |

| Module Assignment | CSN Pin | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **CC1101 Module 1 (433MHz)** | D8 (GPIO 15) | Chip Select 1 |
| **CC1101 Module 2 (315MHz)** | D4 (GPIO 2) | Chip Select 2 |

---

## 4. Navigation & Control Buttons (Active Low)
Wire momentary push buttons between the specified GPIO and Ground (`GND`). Internal pull-ups are handled in software.

| Button Function | ESP8266 GPIO / Pin | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **BTN_NEXT** | D0 (GPIO 16) | Cycle menu forward |
| **BTN_PREV** | D3 (GPIO 0) | Cycle menu backward |
| **BTN_SELECT** | RX (GPIO 3) | Trigger action / Select item |

---

## 5. Infrared (IR) Peripherals
| Component | ESP8266 GPIO / Pin | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **IR Receiver (e.g., )** | D7 (GPIO 13) | Signal input |
| **IR Transmitter LED** | D9 (GPIO 9) | Signal output (include a $\sim 220\Omega$ current-limiting resistor) |
